## Cheat Sheet

### Pages Router — Data Fetching Functions

| Function | Runs when | Use case |
|---|---|---|
| `getStaticProps` | Build time | Static content (SSG) |
| `getStaticPaths` | Build time | Defines dynamic routes for SSG |
| `getServerSideProps` | Every request | Fresh, per-request data (SSR) |
| `useEffect` + `fetch` | In the browser | Client-side, post-load data (CSR) |

### App Router Equivalents (Next.js 13+, `app/` directory)

The newer App Router uses React Server Components; rendering behavior is controlled differently:

```jsx
// app/posts/page.js — static by default
export default async function Posts() {
  const res = await fetch("https://api.example.com/posts"); // cached → SSG-like
  const posts = await res.json();
  return <PostList posts={posts} />;
}
```

```jsx
// Force dynamic (SSR-like) rendering
export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
```

```jsx
// ISR-like revalidation
export const revalidate = 60;
```

